Package: os7-app-softwareupdate
Version: @OS7_VERSION@
Architecture: @OS7_ARCH@
Maintainer: Bastian Wirth <bastian.wirth@upinblue.com>
Section: admin
Priority: optional
Depends: dotnet-runtime-10.0, libfontconfig1, libx11-6, libice6, libsm6, polkitd, os7-module (= @OS7_VERSION@)
Recommends: os7-desktop-theme (= @OS7_VERSION@)
Homepage: https://github.com/upinblue/os7
Description: OS/7 Software Update — the update train, in a window
 The first of OS/7's own graphical applications (docs/GUI-APPS-PLAN.md): what
 the update channel offers, what can be installed on this machine and what
 cannot, why not in each case, and one button that starts it.
 .
 It implements no policy. Every judgement it appears to make is read from
 `Get-OS7Release -Available`, and the update itself runs in a systemd unit that
 calls `Update-OS7` — the same code path an operator gets from PowerShell and
 the same one the unattended timer uses. The window is a second face for one
 mechanism, never a second mechanism.
 .
 It never runs as root. Reading the channel needs no privilege; installing does,
 and that happens by asking systemd to start os7-update@<version>.service, which
 polkit governs — so the operator authenticates in polkit's own dialog and this
 application never sees a password.
 .
 An Avalonia application, framework-dependent against the .NET runtime the image
 already carries. It depends on libfontconfig1 and the X11 libraries explicitly
 rather than inheriting them from ubuntu-desktop-minimal: they arrive on a GUI
 image transitively, and a window that cannot draw a letter is not the way to
 discover that a machine took another path.
 .
 amd64 only. arm64 is server-only and has no desktop.
